{"step_index":122,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T18:31:39Z","thinking":"**Listing Key Assets**\n\nI've got the assets lined up: `google.png`, `landing.png`, `login.png`, `logo.png`, and `pricing-top.png`. I'm going through them now, making sure everything is in order.\n\n\n**Considering Project Structure**\n\nI'm now weighing the best project structure. Initializing Next.js directly in the workspace root could conflict with existing files like 'annotations' and 'brain'. I'm considering using `./` and then verifying the initialization process for this. Options for `npx -y create-next-app@latest` will need to be scoped out, as I assess the best way to handle the structure.\n\n\n**Evaluating Framework Options**\n\nI'm now deep in framework options. Initially, I thought about creating files directly, but Next.js's setup is extensive. Now, I'm leaning toward Vite. It's lighter, quicker to set up, and simpler for a frontend app that communicates with a separate backend.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"node -v","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\ambat\\.gemini\\antigravity","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Checking Node.js version","toolSummary":"Run command"}}]}
